-- title:
--   Uniformiser germ in mathfrak m_z² at singular points of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((q)) =$ `LaurentSeries L` over $L$ given by $K =$ `laurentBaseChange L (x1FunctionField (M*p))`, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M*p))` of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $A$ acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1} \cdot \sum$ `jNumQ`, and assume $j \ne 0$. Let $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the scheme obtained by gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ attached to $\{j\}$ and to $\{j^{-1}\}$ along their common middle chart, and let $z$ be a point of $X$. Let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ through the structure morphism `TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A K j` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and suppose $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_z$ of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ and that the quotient $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}/(\varpi_z)$ is not a regular local ring. Then $\varpi_z \in \mathfrak m_z^2$.
--
--   At a point of the special fibre of this two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ at which that fibre is singular, the uniformiser of the base lies in the square of the maximal ideal; equivalently the local equation of the degeneration is $uv = \varpi$ with thickness one, the classical picture of the crossings of the reduction of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$. It feeds the statement that the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ is proper and flat over $A$ with regular local rings and the expected degeneration into two smooth curves.
